<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shen Baoxu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 506 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shen Baoxu was a minister of the State of Chu who saved it after the invasion by Wu in 506 BCE. When Wu forces occupied the Chu capital Ying, he went to the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> to ask for help and, according to the Zuo zhuan, wept day and night for seven days until Duke Ai of Qin agreed to send an army, which helped drive out the Wu invaders.</p></div>
